# bcm2712_defconfig has 16 KB pages, and Buildroot's toolchain links for
# 4 KB ones: more than half of the image's programs and libraries (Python,
# dbus, ffmpeg, systemd's tools, ...) have segments a 16 KB kernel cannot
# map. Buildroot's own raspberrypi5_defconfig takes 4 KB pages too.
CONFIG_ARM64_4K_PAGES=y
# The defconfig's release suffix is -v8-16k, which uname -r and
# /lib/modules would then show for this 4 KB kernel. -v8 is what Raspberry
# Pi calls its own 4 KB arm64 kernel.
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-v8"
